    "body": "Rail volume hit a new five-year high and the spot-to-contract spread narrowed to its closest level to breakeven since the beginning of October. Rejections jumped 91 basis points to their highest reading since late October. The three-month outlook slips a point to 76.\nThis week’s SONAR Pricing Power Index (PPI): 73 (up from 68).\nThe composite rose five points, with broad gains across capacity and pricing. The rejection rate jumped 91 basis points to 13.68%, moving to the 83rd percentile from the 77th. Van rejections surged to 11.35% from 10.11%. Rail volume hit a new five-year high at 36,665 loaded containers, reaching the 100th percentile from the 99th. The national spot rate rose to $3.61 a mile, moving to the 98th percentile from the 97th, and the spot-to-contract spread narrowed to negative $0.11 in the weekly series from negative $0.23, moving to the 81st percentile from the 76th. Intermodal contract rates moved to the 71st percentile from the 65th. Partly offsetting those gains, accepted truckload volume rose about 2% to 9,810 but remained in the 21st percentile, ocean bookings were essentially flat at 1,856 in the 44th percentile, and van contract rates eased slightly to the 89th percentile from the 90th.\n& Market Monitor Exclusive\nKeep reading with or Market Monitor\nFull access to this article is reserved for\nand Market Monitor customers.\nExisting customers, log in\nLog in to Log in to Market Monitor\nNot a customer yet? Learn more about both platforms →",
